implementationPlan.description:
ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW, once, as the final step. Load adversarial-self-review. Read the diff as an agent trying to mint an authenticated run:

1. Forgery and retargeting:
   - record_check_run runs with copied runnerIds and dispatchIds;
   - squatting a future observation id: identical content is harmless, and differing content becomes CHECK_RUN_IMMUTABLE, so the worst case is denial, not trust;
   - dispatching a superseded candidate;
   - an observation naming any binding field.
2. Atomicity:
   - every refusal ordered before the first write;
   - the CheckRun written before the marker;
   - the R2 retry path;
   - two observations racing under the mutex.
3. Files:
   - the checks/dispatches and checks/observations paths go through writeEntity's traversal guard;
   - case-variant ids on NTFS and APFS;
   - loadEntities never mixing them into checkRuns.
4. Rails:
   - checkRunStore, recordCheckRun and policy byte-unchanged, so legacy policy is identical;
   - no forbidden-pattern tokens;
   - no .moe edits and no Git writes;
   - verified-local untouched.

Write the Serena handoff memory 'task-task-c9fe2515321e4b1a881bb844965fe179-handoff', giving the landed names and codeNames for CQ-V03 (task-9cc13170) and CQ-V04 (task-a9d1a74d).
